WEBVTT

00:07.659 --> 00:09.748
♪ Your heart has called me♪

00:09.879 --> 00:12.664
♪ Closer to you♪

00:12.795 --> 00:15.450
♪ I will be♪

00:15.537 --> 00:16.668
♪ All that you need♪

00:16.842 --> 00:20.107
♪ Just trust...♪

00:20.194 --> 00:24.328
Baby? Lottie?
We're almost there, okay?

00:24.502 --> 00:26.809
Might want to wake up.

00:26.896 --> 00:28.680
♪ Baby, I believe.♪

00:55.272 --> 00:57.100
- Hi, morning.
- Hey, good morning.

00:57.231 --> 00:59.146
- Can I see your license?
- Uh, yes.

01:03.367 --> 01:05.152
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

01:05.239 --> 01:07.067
All right, I'm-a need
to see your bag.

01:07.154 --> 01:08.938
Oh. Okay.

01:15.727 --> 01:17.686
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

01:17.816 --> 01:19.340
All right now.

01:19.470 --> 01:20.732
- Let me see that bag, too.
- You want this bag?

01:20.819 --> 01:23.170
- Yeah, the backpack. Mm-hmm.
- Oh.

01:23.344 --> 01:25.259
Here.

01:25.389 --> 01:27.304
All right. Thank you.

01:34.703 --> 01:37.619
Is this really necessary?
She's just a child.

01:37.793 --> 01:39.621
You'd be surprised
who's snuck guns in here.

01:42.537 --> 01:43.973
- Here we go.
- Thank you.

01:44.147 --> 01:45.496
You got that. Watch yourself.

01:45.627 --> 01:48.282
Have a good day.

01:48.412 --> 01:50.936
You'll need these at all times.
Hold on to that.

01:51.067 --> 01:52.938
- Okay. Thank you.
- Straight up there.

01:53.069 --> 01:54.549
You got it.
Have a good one, now.

02:24.970 --> 02:26.581
Hello, y'all, and welcome

02:26.755 --> 02:29.323
to Kirkwood Chocolate's
one and only Chocolateland.

02:29.453 --> 02:31.760
A studio for the culture
and what...?

02:31.890 --> 02:33.022
By the culture.

02:33.196 --> 02:34.676
- By the culture, that's right.
- Yes, Lord!

02:36.112 --> 02:38.027
Over here we have
Mr. Chocolate's

02:38.114 --> 02:39.463
state-of-the-art film stages.

02:39.637 --> 02:41.813
- What's that over there?
- Uh,

02:41.900 --> 02:44.903
those are Mr. Chocolate's
old stages and studios.

02:45.034 --> 02:47.036
He's converted them
into a personal office.

02:47.254 --> 02:49.908
Mr. Chocolate
is very... private.

02:50.039 --> 02:51.345
So, no one's allowed in

02:51.475 --> 02:54.261
or out.

02:54.435 --> 02:56.176
All right, moving on.

03:06.925 --> 03:08.579
Hi. We're here for filming.

03:08.710 --> 03:10.364
- Hi. Nice to meet you.
- Oh.

03:10.581 --> 03:11.713
- Yes.
- Um, you can just
sign your name.

03:11.930 --> 03:13.715
- Oh, okay.
- You can sign in over there,

03:13.932 --> 03:15.369
and I'll come and bring you
to hair and makeup

03:15.586 --> 03:17.022
when they're ready for you.
If you need anything,

03:17.153 --> 03:18.502
- please ask, okay?
- Thank you.

03:18.633 --> 03:20.287
FIRST P.A.:
No problem.

03:20.417 --> 03:22.202
Okay, ready?

03:22.289 --> 03:23.855
Good.

03:23.942 --> 03:25.640
Take a break, we'll do it again.

03:31.167 --> 03:32.386
Yo, man, don't come at me
with that bullshit.

03:32.516 --> 03:33.735
You know I had to take Chrissy
to set today.

03:33.865 --> 03:35.389
I'm hungry.

03:35.519 --> 03:36.868
Uh-uh, uh-oh.

03:36.999 --> 03:39.958
Oh. Okay, okay.

03:40.176 --> 03:41.830
If that nigga ain't got
my bands, he dead anyway.

03:41.960 --> 03:43.527
I don't think I brought
any snacks. They're in the car.

03:43.745 --> 03:45.486
Nigga, hold that nigga there.

03:45.616 --> 03:47.183
We'll just grab
something after, okay?

03:47.401 --> 03:49.316
Oh, okay. Okay. Nigga,
hold that nigga's ass there.

03:49.446 --> 03:50.752
Hold him there.

03:50.969 --> 03:52.101
Hold that nigga there!
I told you,

03:52.188 --> 03:53.450
put that nigga in the trunk
if you have to.

03:53.537 --> 03:54.756
Hold that nigga there.

03:54.886 --> 03:57.106
- That's a really nice goldfish.
- Thanks.

03:58.455 --> 04:00.240
Shut up, shut up,
shut up, shut up.

04:00.414 --> 04:02.677
Hey, uh, excuse me.

04:02.764 --> 04:04.461
Yo, I'm sorry
for being loud or whatever.

04:04.635 --> 04:06.811
Oh, it's okay.

04:06.985 --> 04:10.424
Um... what's your name?

04:10.554 --> 04:12.121
Denise.

04:12.295 --> 04:13.992
Nice to meet you, Denise.

04:14.123 --> 04:15.907
Yeah.

04:15.994 --> 04:17.648
FIRST P.A.:
Vanessa.

04:17.779 --> 04:19.781
Oh, we're ready for you.

04:21.348 --> 04:24.568
Uh... Denise,
they're ready for you.

04:25.830 --> 04:27.702
Uh, let's pack up.

04:38.103 --> 04:40.018
- Is this your first time here?
- Oh, yeah.

04:40.149 --> 04:41.106
It's great, isn't it?

04:41.237 --> 04:42.238
Yeah, it's fun.

04:42.369 --> 04:44.284
That's the one you saw
with Grandma.

04:59.473 --> 05:01.692
Baby, you want my phone?
You can have it.

05:01.823 --> 05:03.520
I'm okay.

05:05.696 --> 05:07.481
- Mm, she is so sweet.
- Aw.

05:07.611 --> 05:09.265
I can't tell you
how many kids come through

05:09.396 --> 05:11.049
with a diva attitude.

05:11.180 --> 05:12.921
Thank you.

05:13.051 --> 05:15.489
Honestly,
it's your first time on set.

05:15.619 --> 05:16.925
Both of us, actually.

05:17.055 --> 05:18.187
- Really?
- Mm-hmm.

05:18.361 --> 05:20.276
Are you
a Kirkwood Chocolate fan?

05:20.407 --> 05:22.147
Uh... I haven't really

05:22.278 --> 05:25.063
watched his stuff
in a while, so...

05:25.194 --> 05:27.849
Yeah. I hate it, personally.

05:28.023 --> 05:28.850
Oh.

05:29.024 --> 05:30.417
- No offense.
- No.

05:30.634 --> 05:33.289
No, truly, none taken.

05:33.507 --> 05:35.073
Yeah, honestly, I don't know,
it was just, like,

05:35.247 --> 05:37.859
- a quick way to make
some good money, and...
- Yeah.

05:37.946 --> 05:40.078
And we're supporting Black
art, so I thought that was good,

05:40.296 --> 05:41.950
and... my friend, actually,

05:42.080 --> 05:44.082
told me to audition. It made me
feel kind of independent.

05:44.300 --> 05:46.084
- Mm-hmm.
- So, I thought I'd just
sort of follow that.

05:46.258 --> 05:47.521
Yeah. Yeah, I mean,

05:47.695 --> 05:48.957
- I'm doing this
to get my bread up.
- Mm-hmm.

05:49.087 --> 05:50.741
- And it's an experience,
you know?
- Exactly.

05:50.872 --> 05:52.395
- We deserve that.
- Yeah.

05:52.526 --> 05:54.441
And then, I was also, like,
I don't really care,

05:54.571 --> 05:56.399
so I could just have fun,

05:56.530 --> 05:58.662
and then my daughter could see
me do something I wanted to do.

05:58.749 --> 06:00.534
- Yo, air should be working now.
- Oh, good.

06:00.708 --> 06:03.319
Take a second and look
at the hot water.... Oh, uh...

06:03.450 --> 06:05.103
My bad, I didn't mean
to interrupt you guys.

06:05.234 --> 06:07.367
- Oh, no, you're good.
- It's okay.
- Hi, I'm Shamik.

06:07.454 --> 06:10.457
Hi. Vanessa.

06:10.544 --> 06:12.763
I ain't seen you before.
What show you work on?

06:12.894 --> 06:14.591
Uh, I'm just a day player today.

06:14.678 --> 06:16.201
- Oh, really?
- Mm-hmm.

06:16.332 --> 06:18.116
- Well,
it's nice to meet you.
- You, too.

06:18.334 --> 06:20.815
- I'll see you around. All right.
- All right.

06:24.340 --> 06:26.777
Well, okay, Miss Vanessa.

06:26.908 --> 06:28.562
- I see you.
- Copy. Phaedra.

06:28.692 --> 06:30.433
We're gonna need her
in 40 minutes.

06:30.564 --> 06:33.349
Oh, okay.

06:33.480 --> 06:35.046
Girl, we just... in here
talking. Okay, I'm just gonna...

06:43.490 --> 06:45.013
You don't need him.

06:45.143 --> 06:46.928
Sandra, he is not worth it.

06:47.102 --> 06:48.495
But he's my husband.

06:48.669 --> 06:50.932
If I don't stand with him,
who else will?

06:53.500 --> 06:55.502
What the hell is going on here?

06:55.676 --> 06:57.634
Didn't I tell you
you couldn't have any friends?

06:57.808 --> 06:59.506
Charles, I love you,

06:59.680 --> 07:02.030
but a woman has needs
and boundaries.

07:02.160 --> 07:04.293
You represent me
when you walk out of this house.

07:04.380 --> 07:07.470
I don't care what your little
thot friends over there think.

07:07.601 --> 07:08.993
MALE VOICE [over intercom]:
Dramond.

07:14.956 --> 07:17.306
Grab her by the shoulders.

07:20.396 --> 07:23.312
- Who is that?
- Mr. Chocolate.

07:23.486 --> 07:25.619
MR. CHOCOLATE [over intercom]:
Mikey, please mess up her hair.

07:31.189 --> 07:33.104
More, Mikey.

07:38.545 --> 07:40.634
Thank you. Continue.

07:40.808 --> 07:43.071
I'll be damned
if you embarrass me like that

07:43.201 --> 07:44.420
ever again.

07:44.551 --> 07:45.769
Both of you, out.

07:45.943 --> 07:46.857
Charles, we're here...

07:46.988 --> 07:48.642
- Now.
- Shut up.

07:48.772 --> 07:50.339
Baby. You have to be quiet...

07:50.513 --> 07:51.645
MR. CHOCOLATE:
Who said that?

07:51.775 --> 07:54.778
Uh, I'm sorry.
That was my daughter. Um...

07:54.952 --> 07:56.780
Baby, you have to be quiet
when they're filming, okay?

07:56.954 --> 07:58.565
So they can record it.
Okay, mama?

07:58.739 --> 08:00.784
MR. CHOCOLATE:
May I see her?

08:00.958 --> 08:02.046
Uh, I'm sorry, my daughter?

08:02.220 --> 08:04.222
MR. CHOCOLATE:
Yes.

08:04.353 --> 08:06.355
Uh, s-sure.

08:08.879 --> 08:11.099
Where are you?

08:11.229 --> 08:13.144
MR. CHOCOLATE:
I'm everywhere, like God.

08:13.275 --> 08:15.669
I'm Mr. Chocolate.

08:15.886 --> 08:18.933
Why did you
tell that mean man to shut up?

08:19.107 --> 08:20.587
He was being mean.

08:23.720 --> 08:25.374
I like her.
Put her in the scene.

08:25.592 --> 08:26.897
Mikey, place her on the stairs.

08:27.028 --> 08:28.812
Oh, oh, I'm sorry,
she-she doesn't act.

08:29.030 --> 08:30.510
Everyone acts, Miss Vanessa.

08:32.381 --> 08:34.165
What is your name, young lady?

08:34.383 --> 08:36.298
Lottie.

08:36.385 --> 08:38.387
Lottie.

08:38.474 --> 08:39.606
Can you tell the mean man
to shut up

08:39.823 --> 08:42.260
exactly the way you did
the first time?

08:42.391 --> 08:44.045
Okay.

08:44.262 --> 08:45.612
- Wonderful. Dramond...
- Are you gonna be okay?

08:45.829 --> 08:47.831
...take it from,
"I'll be damned."

08:47.962 --> 08:49.616
I'll be damned

08:49.833 --> 08:52.183
if you embarrass me
like that ever again.

08:52.270 --> 08:53.402
Both of you, out.

08:53.620 --> 08:54.621
Charles, we're here supporting...

08:54.751 --> 08:56.057
- Now.
- Shut up.

08:57.841 --> 08:59.930
MR. CHOCOLATE:
Amazing. Cut. Moving on.

09:00.061 --> 09:02.629
Oh, but, Mr. Chocolate, um,

09:02.759 --> 09:04.718
that was just
the blocking rehearsal,

09:04.848 --> 09:06.415
and Lottie's not in
any of the earlier scenes.

09:06.502 --> 09:07.895
We'll fix it in post.

09:07.982 --> 09:09.853
But, sir,

09:09.984 --> 09:11.725
the post department
has been begging us

09:11.855 --> 09:14.075
to fix it in "pre."

09:16.991 --> 09:18.732
Understood, sir.

09:18.862 --> 09:20.995
Call Marcie in costumes. We're
gonna need children's clothes.

09:21.082 --> 09:22.866
I'm sorry,
what-what-what's happening?

09:23.084 --> 09:24.433
Oh, Mr. Chocolate
just needs Lottie

09:24.651 --> 09:25.739
in the next scene.

09:25.869 --> 09:27.392
How long's that gonna take?

09:27.523 --> 09:28.959
With the way that
Mr. Chocolate shoots,

09:29.090 --> 09:31.745
you'll both still probably
be done by lunch,

09:31.875 --> 09:33.442
but we just need
to get her fitted.

09:33.529 --> 09:34.791
Come with me, please.

09:41.450 --> 09:42.756
Can I wear this?

09:42.886 --> 09:45.454
It's up to your mother, darling,

09:45.628 --> 09:47.021
but Mr. Chocolate says
whatever you want.

09:47.108 --> 09:49.589
- This okay?
- Yeah,

09:49.676 --> 09:51.025
that's fine.

09:59.337 --> 10:01.775
You okay, love?
You nervous for her?

10:01.905 --> 10:05.779
Yeah. I guess
I'm kind of nervous.

10:05.953 --> 10:08.477
Well, she seems to be
very excited.

10:08.651 --> 10:10.392
She'll do fine.

10:12.481 --> 10:14.788
Yeah, but I guess, like,
putting children

10:14.918 --> 10:17.486
on screen, you know,
I don't know if she really

10:17.660 --> 10:19.270
understands the bigger picture
of what we're doing,

10:19.444 --> 10:20.794
you know what I mean?

10:20.924 --> 10:22.926
What have you seen
of Mr. Chocolate's?

10:23.057 --> 10:25.363
Not a lot. Um...

10:25.537 --> 10:28.845
I saw that one movie
where the woman marries...

10:29.019 --> 10:30.586
an angel.

10:30.717 --> 10:32.936
Oh, yeah. Do Not Be Afraid.

10:33.067 --> 10:34.285
Yes, yes.

10:34.459 --> 10:37.506
I, um, didn't love that one.

10:37.680 --> 10:38.855
You a Christian?

10:41.162 --> 10:42.598
I'm spiritual.

10:42.729 --> 10:45.470
It's okay.

10:45.601 --> 10:47.037
None of us are perfect.

10:47.211 --> 10:49.823
The only reason I ask
is because it always reminds me

10:49.953 --> 10:51.955
of this verse, "Whoever

10:52.086 --> 10:55.089
"doesn't receive the
Kingdom of God like a child,

10:55.219 --> 10:56.960
won't enter it."

10:57.134 --> 10:59.180
And I always thought
that meant whoever's not open

10:59.354 --> 11:01.530
to the joys of a child--

11:01.748 --> 11:04.054
like their own child--

11:04.185 --> 11:06.100
is not really open
to true happiness.

11:07.971 --> 11:09.320
Mom. Mom.

11:09.451 --> 11:11.322
Looks cool, huh?

11:11.540 --> 11:13.281
Wow.

11:13.411 --> 11:15.849
It looks very cool.

11:15.979 --> 11:18.547
Can I make a video?
I look like Doja Cat.

11:21.289 --> 11:22.812
Listen, Doja.

11:25.293 --> 11:28.209
If you ever feel uncomfortable,

11:28.339 --> 11:29.993
and you want to leave,

11:30.211 --> 11:32.561
you just give me
the "thumbs down" sign,

11:32.692 --> 11:34.432
and we go right then and there.

11:34.563 --> 11:35.564
We don't even have to talk
to anybody, okay?

11:35.782 --> 11:36.870
Okay.

11:37.000 --> 11:38.698
Want to shake on it?

11:41.657 --> 11:44.442
We're ready for Lottie on set.

11:44.573 --> 11:45.835
All right, baby.
Come on, let's go.

11:51.449 --> 11:53.016
I don't like that man, Mama.

11:53.147 --> 11:54.801
I don't like how he treats you.

11:55.018 --> 11:57.804
I know, baby,
but he's all I got.

12:01.024 --> 12:02.809
Your mama's crazy.

12:03.026 --> 12:05.159
If my mama's crazy,

12:05.376 --> 12:07.248
what's your mama?

12:09.816 --> 12:12.557
You better tell her.

12:12.688 --> 12:13.689
MR. CHOCOLATE [over intercom]:
Cut.

12:13.820 --> 12:15.169
Moving on. That was perfect.

12:15.256 --> 12:17.475
Lottie.

12:17.606 --> 12:19.390
Lottie?

12:25.527 --> 12:28.051
She's good.

12:28.182 --> 12:30.837
Thank you.

12:31.011 --> 12:33.361
Honestly, we need
to stick together.

12:33.491 --> 12:36.625
Mr. Chocolate
likes your daughter,

12:36.799 --> 12:39.149
probably writing a kids show
for her right now.

12:40.890 --> 12:41.848
Maybe my daughter
could be the best friend

12:41.978 --> 12:43.980
who's good at computers.

12:44.067 --> 12:45.373
Nah.

12:45.503 --> 12:47.854
She's, uh,
just acting for today.

12:48.028 --> 12:49.420
Honestly, she's not even
really that into acting.

12:49.551 --> 12:51.509
I don't know.

12:51.683 --> 12:53.642
She seems pretty happy.

12:53.816 --> 12:54.774
Yeah, no. She's...

12:54.861 --> 12:57.080
she's not ready.
But your daughter

12:57.254 --> 12:58.429
should have the show.

12:58.603 --> 13:00.518
Oh, I know.

13:00.692 --> 13:02.869
She's not the right "type."

13:02.956 --> 13:05.741
Like I said, we really need
to stick together.

13:09.223 --> 13:10.311
How was that, Mommy?

13:10.441 --> 13:11.312
That was great.

13:11.442 --> 13:14.402
That was great. Yes.

13:14.532 --> 13:15.751
Excuse me, s-- Where's Lottie?

13:15.882 --> 13:17.405
They moved to the next scene.

13:17.535 --> 13:20.190
- Next scene?
- Mm-hmm.

13:20.321 --> 13:21.322
How many more scenes is she in?

13:21.496 --> 13:23.890
Well, she's in...

13:24.064 --> 13:25.674
uh...

13:27.850 --> 13:29.983
14 more scenes,
and it looks like they made her

13:30.113 --> 13:32.637
number three on the call sheet. Congratulations.

13:32.768 --> 13:34.335
Oh, no, no, no.
I think I need

13:34.509 --> 13:35.553
to speak to somebody in charge.

13:35.684 --> 13:37.120
Is Mr. Chocolate around?

13:37.251 --> 13:39.862
No.
He never leaves his office.

13:39.993 --> 13:42.691
I've actually never seen
Mr. Chocolate.

13:42.822 --> 13:43.823
I just know
he's always watching me.

13:45.476 --> 13:47.217
Guy's a genius.

13:47.348 --> 13:50.351
That's fine.
Um, where is Lottie headed?

13:50.525 --> 13:52.092
Tommy Lister Memorial Stage.

13:52.222 --> 13:54.572
- Okay, could you take me there?
- I...

13:54.746 --> 13:57.445
I'll take you, if you want.

13:59.273 --> 14:00.361
So, where you from?

14:00.578 --> 14:03.059
I'm from here. You?

14:03.146 --> 14:05.148
Oh, I'm from New Orleans.

14:05.235 --> 14:07.020
Don't worry, I still like you, though.

14:07.150 --> 14:09.022
Think it's cool seeing a mother

14:09.239 --> 14:11.894
and daughter working together.
How long y'all been acting?

14:12.025 --> 14:14.027
Uh, we actually
don't really act.

14:14.157 --> 14:16.159
A friend of mine put me on,
and I was told

14:16.333 --> 14:18.074
maybe it'd be
a good experience for me.

14:18.161 --> 14:20.947
Oh, well, you guys are great.

14:24.385 --> 14:25.952
How'd you end up
in maintenance here?

14:26.126 --> 14:28.171
I got incarcerated
when I was young.

14:28.389 --> 14:30.130
Two years and...

14:30.260 --> 14:31.958
wasn't a lot of opportunity
when I got out.

14:32.088 --> 14:35.048
Mr. Chocolate,
he had this program.

14:35.178 --> 14:36.179
Just thought
I'd build up my résumé

14:36.397 --> 14:38.181
and work on coding at night.

14:38.399 --> 14:40.749
- Coding?
- Yeah, I got this
crypto mining farm.

14:40.880 --> 14:42.272
It's in my closet.

14:42.403 --> 14:44.274
I've been playing
with solar batteries, too.

14:44.492 --> 14:46.407
Do you even know what that is?
Or am I just, like...

14:46.537 --> 14:47.974
am I mansplaining?

14:48.061 --> 14:49.758
You're doing a little bit
of both, but it's cute enough.

14:49.889 --> 14:52.630
Look, uh, there it is.

14:52.848 --> 14:55.720
- Okay.
- Look, I got to run, but...
you ever got a problem

14:55.851 --> 14:57.070
with your fridge or your phone,

14:57.200 --> 14:58.462
or you just want
to get coffee...

14:58.549 --> 15:00.203
you should hit me.

15:00.421 --> 15:02.684
- Thank you.
- Oh, yeah, for sure.

15:22.356 --> 15:24.967
You white piece of shit.

15:25.098 --> 15:26.926
I hope you get shot
in the theatre.

15:28.840 --> 15:30.016
MR. CHOCOLATE [over intercom]:
And cut. Flip the set.

15:31.147 --> 15:33.584
SECOND P.A.:
Uh, Mr. Chocolate,

15:33.671 --> 15:36.022
that was a blocking.
We weren't filming.

15:36.109 --> 15:37.458
MR. CHOCOLATE:
We'll fix it in post.
Flip the set.

15:37.588 --> 15:38.807
Um, excuse me, Miss? Sorry.

15:38.938 --> 15:40.983
Have you seen my daughter?

15:41.114 --> 15:43.377
She's a little girl with
cornrows? They said she would be

15:43.464 --> 15:45.248
- on this set.
- Uh, I think

15:45.422 --> 15:47.903
they're on the
John Witherspoon Stage now.

15:48.034 --> 15:51.385
Okay, I'm sorry.
This is unacceptable.

15:51.472 --> 15:52.603
Who is with my daughter?

15:52.734 --> 15:54.127
I'm sorry.

15:54.257 --> 15:56.999
I'm directing two pilots
and starring in another.

15:57.130 --> 15:58.827
I just bring people
where he tells me.

15:59.001 --> 16:01.134
Mr. Chocolate is the only person

16:01.264 --> 16:03.484
who actually knows
what's going on.

16:03.614 --> 16:06.052
You need to bring me
to my daughter right now.

16:09.490 --> 16:10.926
- Right now. Yes?
- Okay.

16:11.057 --> 16:12.362
- Thank you.
- Yeah, yeah.

16:12.493 --> 16:14.495
You realize you can't just
take somebody's child

16:14.625 --> 16:17.367
without their permission?
That that's kidnapping?

16:17.498 --> 16:20.457
Ma'am, I'm sorry this happened,

16:20.588 --> 16:23.808
but you won't even remember this
when she wins that BET Award.

16:23.939 --> 16:27.377
Award? This script has a woman
eating a crack sandwich.

16:27.508 --> 16:29.031
Yeah.

16:29.162 --> 16:31.860
- Man, that's good.
- Mr. Chocolate is a wild boy.

16:31.947 --> 16:33.514
What was I even thinking?

16:33.644 --> 16:34.819
I can't believe
I let her do this.

16:34.950 --> 16:36.386
I wouldn't even
let her watch this.

16:36.604 --> 16:38.171
SECOND P.A.:
Well, my kids love it.
It's funny.

16:38.345 --> 16:40.042
Me and my grandma
watch his HIV drama,

16:40.173 --> 16:42.610
Love After Diagnosis,
sometimes after church.

16:42.740 --> 16:44.960
I love his rap musical
about the Black law professor

16:45.091 --> 16:46.527
that kills
all her white students.

16:46.744 --> 16:47.963
Yeah.

16:48.181 --> 16:50.531
- That show is lit.
- Yeah, but it's not good.

16:50.705 --> 16:53.186
I don't know. He won,
like, 30 NAACP Awards

16:53.316 --> 16:55.101
- and a bunch of BET ones.
- Mm-hmm. Yeah.

16:55.275 --> 16:57.407
Yeah, so Black awards.

16:57.538 --> 16:59.540
So, only the white ones
matter to you?

16:59.714 --> 17:01.194
You know what I mean.

17:01.368 --> 17:02.891
Say what you want
about Mr. Chocolate,

17:02.978 --> 17:04.414
- but he's done a lot
for the community.
- SECOND P.A.: Yep.

17:04.545 --> 17:06.460
I'm rooting
for everybody Black.

17:06.547 --> 17:07.461
Mm.

17:07.635 --> 17:09.854
Even O.J.?

17:09.985 --> 17:11.465
- Even O.J.
- Even O.J.

17:12.640 --> 17:15.034
Look, I tried.

17:15.121 --> 17:19.212
Lord knows I tried.

17:19.429 --> 17:21.127
And I don't know
what they said about me,

17:21.344 --> 17:24.652
I don't, I don't know
what you heard, okay?

17:24.782 --> 17:27.481
But sometimes you don't get
the answers you're looking for.

17:27.568 --> 17:29.570
Go ahead and ask me something.

17:29.787 --> 17:32.225
Why am I here, Mama?

17:32.355 --> 17:36.098
None of us asked to be here.

17:36.229 --> 17:38.796
You just go through life
and hope for the best.

17:38.927 --> 17:41.843
But why am I here with you?

17:41.930 --> 17:45.107
Why... didn't you protect me?

17:45.238 --> 17:48.502
Isn't that what mothers
are supposed to do?

17:51.722 --> 17:54.725
This crack sandwich
good as hell.

17:54.812 --> 17:56.684
MR. CHOCOLATE [over intercom]:
Amazing. Moving on.

17:59.078 --> 18:01.732
Lottie? Lottie?

18:09.175 --> 18:10.045
Where is she?

18:10.176 --> 18:12.178
Um...

18:12.352 --> 18:14.397
I'm sorry, ma'am.
I don't know where she is.

18:14.528 --> 18:17.357
But I'm sure she's safe.

18:17.487 --> 18:19.620
Mr. Chocolate
is always watching, and...

18:19.750 --> 18:21.491
he has plans for her.

18:21.622 --> 18:23.276
What the fuck are you saying?
Is this a fucking cult?

18:23.406 --> 18:26.409
Um, e-excuse me, s-security?
I'm sorry, um...

18:26.583 --> 18:28.368
- Mm-hmm?
- I can't find my daughter.

18:28.498 --> 18:29.760
Okay, but I can't actually
help you, though.

18:29.934 --> 18:31.936
You're security.

18:32.067 --> 18:33.503
Uh, technically, but
I'm also just an intern, too.

18:33.634 --> 18:35.766
Here's your coffee.

18:35.853 --> 18:37.333
Thanks.

18:59.442 --> 19:01.575
Give me back my daughter.

19:14.544 --> 19:15.893
MR. CHOCOLATE:
No.

19:23.336 --> 19:25.120
Hell no.

19:30.256 --> 19:32.258
Hey. Hey, love.

19:34.608 --> 19:36.697
You okay?

19:36.871 --> 19:38.133
♪ Uh♪

19:38.307 --> 19:41.136
♪ I do as I want,
I do as I like♪

19:41.310 --> 19:43.051
♪ I no watch face, I no fear♪

19:43.138 --> 19:45.923
♪ Nobody, nobody...♪

19:46.054 --> 19:47.447
Hey!

19:47.577 --> 19:50.493
Kirkwood has my daughter.
I need to see her.

19:50.580 --> 19:52.930
- This is a private
residence, ma'am.
- Okay, this is ridiculous.

19:53.148 --> 19:55.281
He has my daughter,
and I'm gonna get in there.

19:55.368 --> 19:56.369
Ma'am, we're gonna call
the police.

19:56.499 --> 19:58.501
You know what? Call the police.
I want them here.

19:58.719 --> 20:00.242
- Give me my daughter.
- It's okay, it's okay.

20:00.373 --> 20:01.939
- No. No, no, no.
- It's okay, it's okay.

20:02.157 --> 20:03.941
- Tell me what's happening.
- Kirkwood has my daughter,

20:04.072 --> 20:06.248
and nobody's fucking
helping me find her!

20:06.466 --> 20:07.945
- And I don't know what to do
'cause nobody's helping me.
- It's okay. Shh...

20:08.076 --> 20:10.513
- I just need...
- It's okay, it's okay.

20:10.644 --> 20:13.603
- Okay. Okay, okay. Okay.
- I got you. Don't you worry.

20:13.734 --> 20:16.519
Okay.

20:16.737 --> 20:18.086
Let her in.

20:18.173 --> 20:20.088
She has no clearance, ma'am.
This is Mr. Chocolate's

20:20.306 --> 20:22.656
- personal space.
- Mm. Okay.

20:26.312 --> 20:27.965
Oh, shit.

20:28.096 --> 20:33.319
Ma'am, these are fake M16s
from the film War of God.

20:33.449 --> 20:35.973
Please don't shoot me.

20:36.104 --> 20:37.323
Go in, baby.

20:37.453 --> 20:39.194
♪ Point and kill♪

20:39.325 --> 20:41.631
♪ You can't stop me, oh...♪

20:41.762 --> 20:43.242
♪ You can't stop me,
point and kill.♪

20:43.416 --> 20:45.461
Okay.

20:54.122 --> 20:56.037
:
Mr. Chocolate?

22:05.759 --> 22:07.326
Oh, hello.

22:10.633 --> 22:12.983
I was just writing
on my "Key-iano."

22:13.070 --> 22:15.421
Scripts are like music to me.

22:18.075 --> 22:20.208
Steve Jobs made that for me.

22:22.645 --> 22:26.083
I think of him
every time I write.

22:37.356 --> 22:39.009
Would you like a grit?

22:39.183 --> 22:41.664
Where's my daughter?

22:41.795 --> 22:43.884
She's right there.

22:44.014 --> 22:46.234
On the Mario Van Peebles Stage.

22:46.365 --> 22:49.585
By the time you get there,

22:49.672 --> 22:51.935
she'll have moved on
to the next scene...

22:53.807 --> 22:55.156
...and the next stage.

22:55.243 --> 22:57.027
Where is the next stage?

23:00.248 --> 23:01.510
I don't know.

23:03.904 --> 23:06.036
This whole operation

23:06.254 --> 23:07.734
runs on its own.

23:09.126 --> 23:12.478
I do not understand its...

23:12.608 --> 23:14.262
wants and needs,

23:14.349 --> 23:17.047
nor do I control them.

23:17.134 --> 23:19.354
Chocolateland is my child.

23:20.921 --> 23:22.923
I protect her,

23:23.053 --> 23:24.490
guide her,

23:24.707 --> 23:26.535
but she is not my own.

23:31.279 --> 23:34.238
Have her say,
"But I'm pregnant."

23:34.413 --> 23:36.850
FIRST P.A. [over intercom]:
But this is a kids' show,
Mr. Chocolate.

23:37.024 --> 23:38.634
Thank you.

23:40.070 --> 23:41.507
I'm calling the police.

23:41.681 --> 23:43.291
I own the police.

23:43.422 --> 23:44.945
And most of College Park.

23:45.119 --> 23:46.381
You can't just
take somebody's...

23:46.512 --> 23:48.514
I can do whatever I want!

23:48.644 --> 23:50.472
You break into my cube,

23:50.603 --> 23:53.519
shoot my guard, and then
tell me how to raise my child?!

23:53.649 --> 23:54.955
This is an open carry state,
Ms. Vanessa.

23:55.085 --> 23:56.304
You know, someone as you...

24:01.875 --> 24:03.964
I'm fine.

24:05.966 --> 24:07.620
Grits don't work on me.

24:08.969 --> 24:11.188
I've developed a tolerance
over the years.

24:12.233 --> 24:14.670
Oh, my God.

24:14.844 --> 24:16.193
You're a con man.

24:17.238 --> 24:18.631
You just make unrelatable

24:18.761 --> 24:21.285
shit that takes advantage
of the people

24:21.416 --> 24:23.679
- you say you're trying to help.
- Mr. Chocolate?

24:23.853 --> 24:25.855
Oh, my God. Baby? Baby!

24:25.986 --> 24:27.770
- It's an honor, sir.
- Are you okay?

24:27.944 --> 24:29.293
- Oh, so...
- Yeah, it was fun.

24:29.424 --> 24:32.775
- Everyone said that I was funny.
- Really? Are you okay?

24:32.949 --> 24:34.647
- Yeah.
- You okay?

24:34.777 --> 24:36.300
Uh, Ms. Keifer,

24:36.431 --> 24:38.259
- could you please sign
this time sheet?
- Absolutely not.

24:38.433 --> 24:42.002
"Unrelatable shit," you say.

24:42.176 --> 24:45.135
You know, I've been
watching you, Ms. Keifer.

24:47.094 --> 24:50.097
You're a single mother who can't
afford to feed your daughter.

24:50.227 --> 24:53.317
Phaedra is your
"hip girlfriend."

24:53.448 --> 24:55.363
You have a
"formally incarcerated,

24:55.581 --> 24:57.800
light-skinned love interest,"

24:57.931 --> 25:00.803
a "Christian,
gun-toting grandmother,"

25:00.934 --> 25:03.153
and let me guess,

25:03.240 --> 25:05.025
you have a dark-skinned
baby daddy?

25:05.242 --> 25:07.157
He's brown-skinned.

25:07.244 --> 25:09.812
And you threw grits at me.

25:10.030 --> 25:12.380
Unprovoked.

25:12.511 --> 25:14.600
Face it, Vanessa,

25:14.817 --> 25:17.037
you're
a Kirkwood Chocolate woman.

25:19.692 --> 25:22.825
Well, maybe I am, but that
doesn't make you an artist.

25:23.043 --> 25:24.392
It doesn't.

25:24.479 --> 25:26.263
It makes me a philanthropist.

25:27.613 --> 25:29.484
And I'd like
to make Lottie an offer.

25:29.615 --> 25:31.617
Six seasons
of a children's show.

25:31.704 --> 25:32.835
That would make her
financially stable

25:33.053 --> 25:34.924
until she was 20.
What do you say?

25:35.055 --> 25:36.839
Well, I'm not like one
of those mothers downstairs

25:36.926 --> 25:37.927
that's gonna make
their daughter do something

25:38.058 --> 25:38.928
they don't want to do.

25:39.059 --> 25:40.364
I want to do it.

25:40.495 --> 25:43.063
I want to be
on Mr. Chocolate's show.

25:49.417 --> 25:50.723
:
No.

25:50.853 --> 25:52.725
- No! No!
- Lottie.

25:52.942 --> 25:54.509
- Lottie. Please, Lottie.
- She wants to stay.
- No!

25:54.640 --> 25:56.293
- She wants to stay.
- No!

25:56.424 --> 25:58.165
- She doesn't.
- No!

25:58.295 --> 25:59.645
She can't be not-18 forever.

25:59.862 --> 26:02.430
Lottie. Please, Lottie.

26:02.517 --> 26:03.953
- We have to...
- I shall have her.

26:04.084 --> 26:06.086
She'll be

26:06.173 --> 26:08.175
"Spurned Woman Number Eight"
when I'm done with her!

26:08.305 --> 26:10.351
Lottie, please.

26:12.092 --> 26:14.529
I've lost a lot of blood,
Mikey. Could you please, um...

26:14.660 --> 26:16.009
- Could you call an ambulance?
- Oh, sir. Of course. Um...

26:28.238 --> 26:31.111
Lottie. Come here.

26:37.117 --> 26:39.162
Baby, I want to talk
about what happened, okay?

26:39.336 --> 26:41.382
No.

26:46.909 --> 26:50.913
I know you were having a lot
of fun today.

26:51.044 --> 26:53.873
And...

26:54.003 --> 26:57.703
I'm really sorry
that it ended how it ended, hmm?

26:59.052 --> 27:01.576
But you represent something.

27:01.707 --> 27:06.015
And I know it isn't fair, but
what you do-- it matters a lot.

27:06.146 --> 27:09.236
And... I just really want you
to be old enough

27:09.366 --> 27:11.499
to decide what you want
to represent, okay?

27:11.673 --> 27:13.632
'Cause I...
I can't always protect you.

27:18.288 --> 27:19.725
I'm sorry.

27:23.467 --> 27:25.165
I'm really sorry.

27:26.732 --> 27:28.864
It shouldn't have happened
like that.

27:36.524 --> 27:41.181
Oh. I love you, baby.

27:41.311 --> 27:43.400
You, too.

27:43.618 --> 27:45.533
I'm always gonna be here
for you, okay?

27:45.707 --> 27:47.666
Okay.

28:20.437 --> 28:22.135
I'm gonna make mac and cheese.

28:22.309 --> 28:24.006
Okay.

28:27.227 --> 28:28.794
♪ 3:00 on the dot♪

28:29.011 --> 28:31.013
♪ He pull up on my block♪

28:31.144 --> 28:32.798
♪ We goin' to the mall♪

28:33.015 --> 28:35.322
♪ I'm getting' Nike Shox♪

28:35.539 --> 28:38.760
♪ No, I'm not Baroque but
he treats me like he's Bach♪

28:38.891 --> 28:40.806
♪ I take a little off the top♪

28:40.936 --> 28:43.547
♪ He my dog, Iggy Pop♪

28:43.678 --> 28:45.680
♪ Shopping bag, it's Goyard♪

28:45.811 --> 28:47.769
♪ You lookin' mad, I go hard♪

28:47.900 --> 28:49.902
♪ I'm on a yacht, no lifeguard♪

28:50.032 --> 28:51.555
♪ You not my man,
you a blowhard♪

28:51.686 --> 28:55.342
♪ He givin' me the keys
to the brand-new Benz♪

28:55.472 --> 28:59.520
♪ We chillin' waterfront
but we're not holding hands♪

28:59.607 --> 29:01.478
♪ Wishy washy♪

29:01.609 --> 29:05.134
♪ Not my boyfriend but
I let you take me shopping♪

29:05.265 --> 29:07.963
♪ Buy me what I want,
I want it all♪

29:08.050 --> 29:10.052
♪ Wishy washy♪

29:10.226 --> 29:12.838
♪ I like the attention
but don't get too comfy♪

29:13.012 --> 29:14.491
♪ Wishy washy♪

29:14.622 --> 29:16.058
♪ Wish, wishy♪

29:16.232 --> 29:17.059
♪ Wishy washy♪

29:17.233 --> 29:19.061
♪ Wish, wishy washy♪

29:19.235 --> 29:21.063
♪ Wishy washy♪

29:21.194 --> 29:23.370
♪ Wish, wishy washy.♪

